8. openNURBS (exact-Brep helper, Linux and Windows packages)
------------------------------------------------------------
Use: Narwhal's own ONBREP helper (`narwhal3d/kernel/bin/brep_writer-linux-x86_64`, source `native/brep_writer/main.cpp`, GPL-3.0-or-later) is statically linked with openNURBS to store exact multi-face solids in `.3dm` and in the live document. It runs as a separate process. The Windows package carries the same helper as `narwhal3d/kernel/bin/brep_writer-win32-amd64.exe`, built by `scripts/build_brep_writer_windows.ps1`, which also statically links openNURBS.
Source: https://github.com/mcneel/opennurbs at revision `eb92af3ba1806b0a34a99aba0d3bda83e3d46083`, built by `scripts/build_brep_writer_source.sh` in the pinned manylinux container. The Windows executable is built by `scripts/build_brep_writer_windows.ps1` at the same pinned openNURBS revision.
License: the openNURBS license text, including its bundled zlib notice, is in `licenses/openNURBS-LICENSE.txt`. The official openNURBS documentation describes use as unrestricted while the repository `LICENSE` file says "All Rights Reserved"; the project owner decided on 2026-11-02 to redistribute the helper on the basis of the official documentation. The macOS package does not include the helper yet.

9. Components not included in the public bundle
------------------------------------------------

- CDR generations outside the embedded range can still use an optional local TraceDraw CLI fallback. Development runtime staging pins and verifies the same revision, but the executable is not bundled.
- Inkscape, Poppler, Ghostscript, LibreOffice, and the TraceDraw CLI are not included. Features requiring them report the missing optional dependency; they do not claim those tools are bundled.

